<title>FRANCE: G des Eaux to cut 97 debt by 13 bln ffr.</title>
<headline>G des Eaux to cut 97 debt by 13 bln ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Generale des Eaux will cut its debt by 13 billion francs to 32 billion francs by the end of 1997, chairman Jean-Marie Messier told a news conference on Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared to a debt of 52 billion francs at the end of 1995, he said. Shareholders' funds would be raised by at least 10 billion francs to 43 billion and the debt ratio would be cut to 75 percent at end 1997 from 170 percent at the end of 1995.</p>
</text>
